IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, ss 28, 29 and 29A (change of name; omission of "Limited" or "Berhad").
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). s 28(3C) is shown "[Deleted by Act 36 of 2014]" and is not encoded (NOTES.md, coverage table).
-- Where the text says "to the satisfaction of the Registrar" or "if the Registrar is satisfied", that satisfaction is a plain input: the Registrar's judgment is not guessed.
-- Answers: JUST TRUE (the test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say). See the header of sgi-capacity.l4.

§ `Section 28(1) and (2): changing the name`

-- (1): "A company may by special resolution resolve that its name should be changed to a name by which the company could be registered under section 27(1), (1A) or (1B)."
-- src:5015 | 28.—(1) A company may by special resolution resolve that its
-- src:5016 | name should be changed to a name by which the company could be
-- src:5017 | registered under section 27(1), (1A) or (1B).
@ref s 28(1) (src:5015-5017)
GIVEN `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new name is a name by which the company could be registered under section 27(1), (1A) or (1B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(1) the company may resolve that its name should be changed to the new name` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a special resolution` AND `the new name is a name by which the company could be registered under section 27(1), (1A) or (1B)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may by special resolution resolve that its name should be changed to a name by which the company could be registered under section 27(1), (1A) or (1B)" -- a permission whose method or object is not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- (2): "If the Registrar approves the name which the company has resolved should be its new name, the Registrar must register the company under the new name and issue to the company a notice of incorporation of the company under the new name and, upon the issue of such notice, the change of name becomes effective."
-- The Registrar's duty is read for what it means to the company: it is to be registered and given the notice. A duty gated by "If": JUST FALSE where the gate fails (limit 2 of the grant ruling; fork line F-I21).
-- src:5021 | (2) If the Registrar approves the name which the company has
-- src:5022 | resolved should be its new name, the Registrar must register the
-- src:5023 | company under the new name and issue to the company a notice of
-- src:5024 | incorporation of the company under the new name and, upon the issue
-- src:5025 | of such notice, the change of name becomes effective.
@ref s 28(2) (src:5021-5025)
GIVEN `the Registrar approves the name which the company has resolved should be its new name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) the Registrar must register the company under the new name and issue the notice of incorporation` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar approves the name which the company has resolved should be its new name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Registrar approves the name ..., the Registrar must register the company under the new name and issue to the company a notice of incorporation" (a duty gated by "If": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; fork line F-I21)

-- src:5021 | (2) If the Registrar approves the name which the company has
-- src:5022 | resolved should be its new name, the Registrar must register the
-- src:5023 | company under the new name and issue to the company a notice of
-- src:5024 | incorporation of the company under the new name and, upon the issue
-- src:5025 | of such notice, the change of name becomes effective.
@ref s 28(2) (src:5021-5025)
GIVEN `the Registrar approves the name which the company has resolved should be its new name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has issued the notice of incorporation of the company under the new name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was issued` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(2) the change of name has become effective` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar approves the name which the company has resolved should be its new name`
      AND `the Registrar has issued the notice of incorporation of the company under the new name`
      AND `the date asked` AT LEAST `the day the notice was issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Registrar approves the name ..., ... upon the issue of such notice, the change of name becomes effective" (a status gated by "If" and "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I21)

§ `Section 28(3) to (3E): a name that must not stand`

-- (3): "Despite anything in this section and section 27, if the name of a company is, whether through inadvertence or otherwise or whether originally or by a change of name — (a) a name that is not permitted to be registered under section 27(1)(a), (b) or (d); (b) a name that is not permitted to be registered under section 27(1A) until the expiry of the relevant period ...;
-- (c) a name that is permitted to be registered under section 27(1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period ...; (d) a name that so nearly resembles the name of another company ... as to be likely to be mistaken for it; or (e) a name the use of which has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- the company may by special resolution change its name to a name that is not referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) and, if the Registrar so directs, must so change it within 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow, unless the direction is annulled by the Minister."
-- First limb: the permission. A "may" gated by "if": NOTHING where a gate fails (grant ruling, limit 1; fork line F-I2).
-- src:5027 | (3) Despite anything in this section and section 27, if the name of a
-- src:5028 | company is, whether through inadvertence or otherwise or whether
-- src:5029 | originally or by a change of name —
-- src:5031 | (a) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5032 | section 27(1)(a), (b) or (d);
-- src:5034 | (b) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5035 | section 27(1A) until the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:5036 | mentioned in that section;
-- src:5038 | (c) a name that is permitted to be registered under
-- src:5039 | section 27(1B) only after the expiry of the relevant
-- src:5040 | period mentioned in that section;
-- src:5042 | (d) a name that so nearly resembles the name of another
-- src:5043 | company, or a corporation, limited liability partnership,
-- src:5044 | limited partnership or a registered business name of any
-- src:5045 | person as to be likely to be mistaken for it; or
-- src:5047 | (e) a name the use of which has been restrained by an
-- src:5048 | injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- src:5050 | the company may by special resolution change its name to a name
-- src:5051 | that is not referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) and, if the
-- src:5052 | Registrar so directs, must so change it within 6 weeks after the date of
-- src:5057 | the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow, unless
-- src:5058 | the direction is annulled by the Minister.
@ref s 28(3) (src:5027-5058)
GIVEN `the name of the company is a name not permitted to be registered under section 27(1)(a), (b) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the company is a name not permitted to be registered under section 27(1A) until the expiry of the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the company is a name permitted to be registered under section 27(1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the company so nearly resembles the name of another company, or a corporation, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or a registered business name of any person as to be likely to be mistaken for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use of the name of the company has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new name is a name that is not referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3) the company may by special resolution change its name` MEANS
    IF    (    `the name of the company is a name not permitted to be registered under section 27(1)(a), (b) or (d)`
            OR `the name of the company is a name not permitted to be registered under section 27(1A) until the expiry of the relevant period`
            OR `the name of the company is a name permitted to be registered under section 27(1B) only after the expiry of the relevant period`
            OR `the name of the company so nearly resembles the name of another company, or a corporation, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or a registered business name of any person as to be likely to be mistaken for it`
            OR `the use of the name of the company has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998`)
      AND `the resolution is a special resolution`
      AND `the new name is a name that is not referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the name of a company is ... (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) ...; or (e) ..., the company may by special resolution change its name to a name that is not referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)" -- a power whose "if" gate or method failed (grant ruling, limit 1; fork line F-I2)

-- Second limb: "if the Registrar so directs, must so change it within 6 weeks ... unless the direction is annulled by the Minister." The duty applies only where the name is within (a) to (e), the Registrar has directed and the Minister has not annulled the direction.
-- A duty gated by "if": JUST FALSE where the gate fails (grant ruling, limit 2); once the "unless" is met the text is silent (NOTHING; fork lines F-I21 and F-I18).
-- src:5027 | (3) Despite anything in this section and section 27, if the name of a
-- src:5028 | company is, whether through inadvertence or otherwise or whether
-- src:5029 | originally or by a change of name —
-- src:5031 | (a) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5032 | section 27(1)(a), (b) or (d);
-- src:5034 | (b) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5035 | section 27(1A) until the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:5036 | mentioned in that section;
-- src:5038 | (c) a name that is permitted to be registered under
-- src:5039 | section 27(1B) only after the expiry of the relevant
-- src:5040 | period mentioned in that section;
-- src:5042 | (d) a name that so nearly resembles the name of another
-- src:5043 | company, or a corporation, limited liability partnership,
-- src:5044 | limited partnership or a registered business name of any
-- src:5045 | person as to be likely to be mistaken for it; or
-- src:5047 | (e) a name the use of which has been restrained by an
-- src:5048 | injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- src:5050 | the company may by special resolution change its name to a name
-- src:5051 | that is not referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) and, if the
-- src:5052 | Registrar so directs, must so change it within 6 weeks after the date of
-- src:5057 | the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow, unless
-- src:5058 | the direction is annulled by the Minister.
@ref s 28(3) (src:5027-5058)
GIVEN `the name of the company is a name referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has directed the company to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has annulled the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks after the direction` MEANS
    IF `the name of the company is a name referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)` AND `the Registrar has directed the company to change its name`
    THEN (IF `the Minister has annulled the direction`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the direction is annulled by the Minister" -- once met, the duty is gone and the text says nothing of the company's position (fork line F-I18)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the name of a company is ... and, if the Registrar so directs, must so change it" (a duty gated by "if": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; fork line F-I21)

-- src:5027 | (3) Despite anything in this section and section 27, if the name of a
-- src:5028 | company is, whether through inadvertence or otherwise or whether
-- src:5029 | originally or by a change of name —
-- src:5031 | (a) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5032 | section 27(1)(a), (b) or (d);
-- src:5034 | (b) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5035 | section 27(1A) until the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:5036 | mentioned in that section;
-- src:5038 | (c) a name that is permitted to be registered under
-- src:5039 | section 27(1B) only after the expiry of the relevant
-- src:5040 | period mentioned in that section;
-- src:5042 | (d) a name that so nearly resembles the name of another
-- src:5043 | company, or a corporation, limited liability partnership,
-- src:5044 | limited partnership or a registered business name of any
-- src:5045 | person as to be likely to be mistaken for it; or
-- src:5047 | (e) a name the use of which has been restrained by an
-- src:5048 | injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- src:5050 | the company may by special resolution change its name to a name
-- src:5051 | that is not referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) and, if the
-- src:5052 | Registrar so directs, must so change it within 6 weeks after the date of
-- src:5057 | the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow, unless
-- src:5058 | the direction is annulled by the Minister.
@ref s 28(3) (src:5027-5058)
GIVEN `the day of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 28(3) the last day for compliance` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` AND (`the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the direction` 6 Weeks)
    THEN `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed`
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the direction` 6 Weeks

-- Whether the company has complied (the duty above presupposed): changed within the time: JUST TRUE; changed late, or not changed after the last day: JUST FALSE; not changed and the last day not yet run out: NOTHING.
-- src:5027 | (3) Despite anything in this section and section 27, if the name of a
-- src:5028 | company is, whether through inadvertence or otherwise or whether
-- src:5029 | originally or by a change of name —
-- src:5031 | (a) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5032 | section 27(1)(a), (b) or (d);
-- src:5034 | (b) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5035 | section 27(1A) until the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:5036 | mentioned in that section;
-- src:5038 | (c) a name that is permitted to be registered under
-- src:5039 | section 27(1B) only after the expiry of the relevant
-- src:5040 | period mentioned in that section;
-- src:5042 | (d) a name that so nearly resembles the name of another
-- src:5043 | company, or a corporation, limited liability partnership,
-- src:5044 | limited partnership or a registered business name of any
-- src:5045 | person as to be likely to be mistaken for it; or
-- src:5047 | (e) a name the use of which has been restrained by an
-- src:5048 | injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- src:5050 | the company may by special resolution change its name to a name
-- src:5051 | that is not referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) and, if the
-- src:5052 | Registrar so directs, must so change it within 6 weeks after the date of
-- src:5057 | the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow, unless
-- src:5058 | the direction is annulled by the Minister.
@ref s 28(3) (src:5027-5058)
GIVEN `the day of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A DATE
      `the company has changed its name as directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company changed its name` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3) the company has complied with the direction` MEANS
    IF `the company has changed its name as directed`
    THEN (IF `the day the company changed its name` AT MOST `s 28(3) the last day for compliance` `the day of the direction` `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must so change it within 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `s 28(3) the last day for compliance` `the day of the direction` `the Registrar has allowed a longer period` `the last day of the longer period the Registrar has allowed`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the period has run and the name is not changed
          ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period has not run, and the text does not say the duty is met or unmet before then

DECLARE `s 28(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 28(3) change the company's name as the Registrar has directed`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. Time 0 is the date of the direction; the days allowed are 42 (6 weeks) or the longer period the Registrar allows.
-- src:5027 | (3) Despite anything in this section and section 27, if the name of a
-- src:5028 | company is, whether through inadvertence or otherwise or whether
-- src:5029 | originally or by a change of name —
-- src:5031 | (a) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5032 | section 27(1)(a), (b) or (d);
-- src:5034 | (b) a name that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:5035 | section 27(1A) until the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:5036 | mentioned in that section;
-- src:5038 | (c) a name that is permitted to be registered under
-- src:5039 | section 27(1B) only after the expiry of the relevant
-- src:5040 | period mentioned in that section;
-- src:5042 | (d) a name that so nearly resembles the name of another
-- src:5043 | company, or a corporation, limited liability partnership,
-- src:5044 | limited partnership or a registered business name of any
-- src:5045 | person as to be likely to be mistaken for it; or
-- src:5047 | (e) a name the use of which has been restrained by an
-- src:5048 | injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998,
-- src:5050 | the company may by special resolution change its name to a name
-- src:5051 | that is not referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) and, if the
-- src:5052 | Registrar so directs, must so change it within 6 weeks after the date of
-- src:5057 | the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow, unless
-- src:5058 | the direction is annulled by the Minister.
@ref s 28(3) (src:5027-5058)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the company has to comply, being 42 or the longer period the Registrar allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 28(3) act`
`s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks of the direction` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 28(3) change the company's name as the Registrar has directed`
    WITHIN `the number of days the company has to comply, being 42 or the longer period the Registrar allows`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not change its name within 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the Registrar allowed"

-- (3AA): "The Registrar must not direct a change of name under subsection (3) on the ground that the name of the company could not be registered without contravention of section 27(1)(c)."
-- A bar on the Registrar: JUST TRUE where the ground is section 27(1)(c). Any other ground is outside the bar (NOTHING).
-- src:5062 | (3AA) The Registrar must not direct a change of name under
-- src:5063 | subsection (3) on the ground that the name of the company could not
-- src:5064 | be registered without contravention of section 27(1)(c).
@ref s 28(3AA) (src:5062-5064)
GIVEN `the ground is that the name of the company could not be registered without contravention of section 27(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3AA) the Registrar is barred from directing a change of name under subsection (3) on the ground` MEANS
    IF `the ground is that the name of the company could not be registered without contravention of section 27(1)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not direct a change of name under subsection (3) on the ground that ... section 27(1)(c)" -- the bar names one ground and says nothing of any other

-- (3A), first limb: "Any person may apply in writing to the Registrar to give a direction to a company under subsection (3) on a ground referred to in that subsection".
-- src:5068 | (3A) Any person may apply in writing to the Registrar to give a
-- src:5069 | direction to a company under subsection (3) on a ground referred to in
-- src:5070 | that subsection; but the Registrar must not consider any application to
-- src:5071 | give a direction to a company on the ground referred to in
-- src:5072 | subsection (3)(d) unless the Registrar receives the application
-- src:5073 | within 12 months from the date of change of name of the company.
@ref s 28(3A) (src:5068-5073)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is on a ground referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3A) the person may apply to the Registrar for a direction to the company` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in writing` AND `the application is on a ground referred to in subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person may apply in writing ... on a ground referred to in that subsection" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- (3A), second limb: "the Registrar must not consider any application ... on the ground referred to in subsection (3)(d) unless the Registrar receives the application within 12 months from the date of change of name of the company."
-- A bar: JUST TRUE means the Registrar must not consider the application. Within the 12 months the bar is lifted and the text is silent (NOTHING; fork line F-I18).
-- src:5068 | (3A) Any person may apply in writing to the Registrar to give a
-- src:5069 | direction to a company under subsection (3) on a ground referred to in
-- src:5070 | that subsection; but the Registrar must not consider any application to
-- src:5071 | give a direction to a company on the ground referred to in
-- src:5072 | subsection (3)(d) unless the Registrar receives the application
-- src:5073 | within 12 months from the date of change of name of the company.
@ref s 28(3A) (src:5068-5073)
GIVEN `the application is on the ground referred to in subsection (3)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the change of name of the company` IS A DATE
      `the day the Registrar received the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3A) the Registrar is barred from considering the application` MEANS
    IF    `the application is on the ground referred to in subsection (3)(d)`
      AND `the day the Registrar received the application` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the change of name of the company` 12 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not consider any application ... on the ground referred to in subsection (3)(d) unless the Registrar receives the application within 12 months" -- the bar reaches that ground only; within the 12 months the text is silent (fork line F-I18)

-- (3B): "If the company fails to comply with subsection (3), the company and its officers shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty."
-- src:5077 | (3B) If the company fails to comply with subsection (3), the
-- src:5078 | company and its officers shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:5079 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a
-- src:5080 | default penalty.
@ref s 28(3B) (src:5077-5080)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3B) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with subsection (3)` AND `the person is the company or an officer of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company fails to comply with subsection (3), the company and its officers shall be guilty of an offence" (the provision's own question; split site (i), fork line F-I10)

-- src:5077 | (3B) If the company fails to comply with subsection (3), the
-- src:5078 | company and its officers shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:5079 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a
-- src:5080 | default penalty.
@ref s 28(3B) (src:5077-5080)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 28(3B) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 28(3B) the person is guilty of the offence` `the company fails to comply with subsection (3)` `the person is the company or an officer of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $2,000 "and also to a default penalty"; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for a person it makes guilty

DECLARE `s 28(3D) decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 28(3D)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (3)`
    `s 28(3D)(b) the Registrar's refusal to give a direction to a company under subsection (3) pursuant to an application under subsection (3A)`
    `s 28(3D) another decision`

-- (3D): "An appeal to the Minister against the following decisions of the Registrar that are made on or after 3 January 2016 may be made by the following persons within the following times:
-- (a) ... by the company aggrieved by the decision within 30 days after the decision; (b) ... by the applicant aggrieved by the refusal within 30 days after being informed of the refusal."
-- Same reading as s 27(5): the right person outside 30 days is JUST FALSE (periods ruling, item (a)); another person, another decision, or a decision made before 3 January 2016 is NOTHING.
-- src:5084 | (3D) An appeal to the Minister against the following decisions of
-- src:5085 | the Registrar that are made on or after 3 January 2016 may be made
-- src:5086 | by the following persons within the following times:
-- src:5088 | (a) in the case of the Registrar’s decision under
-- src:5089 | subsection (3) — by the company aggrieved by the
-- src:5090 | decision within 30 days after the decision;
-- src:5092 | (b) in the case of the Registrar’s refusal to give a direction to a
-- src:5093 | company under subsection (3) pursuant to an application
-- src:5094 | under subsection (3A) — by the applicant aggrieved by the
-- src:5095 | refusal within 30 days after being informed of the refusal.
@ref s 28(3D) (src:5084-5095)
GIVEN decision IS A `s 28(3D) decision`
      `the person is the company aggrieved by the decision, or the applicant aggrieved by the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Registrar made the decision` IS A DATE
      `the day the applicant was informed of the refusal` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3D) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` MEANS
    IF decision EQUALS `s 28(3D) another decision`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3D) lists two decisions and says nothing of any other
    ELSE (IF `the day the Registrar made the decision` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "decisions of the Registrar that are made on or after 3 January 2016" -- an earlier decision is outside the subsection
          ELSE (IF `the person is the company aggrieved by the decision, or the applicant aggrieved by the refusal`
                THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` (IF decision EQUALS `s 28(3D)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (3)` THEN `the day the Registrar made the decision` ELSE `the day the applicant was informed of the refusal`) `the day the appeal is made` 30 Days
                      THEN JUST TRUE
                      ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after the decision" / "within 30 days after being informed of the refusal" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the company aggrieved by the decision" / "by the applicant aggrieved by the refusal" -- the text names no other person

-- src:5099 | (3DA) The decision of the Minister on an appeal made under
-- src:5100 | subsection (3D) is final.
@ref s 28(3DA) (src:5099-5100)
GIVEN `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal made under subsection (3D)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3DA) the decision of the Minister on the appeal is final` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal made under subsection (3D)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The decision of the Minister on an appeal made under subsection (3D) is final." says nothing of any other decision

-- src:5104 | (3E) To avoid doubt, where the Registrar makes a decision under
-- src:5105 | subsection (3) or the Minister makes a decision under
-- src:5106 | subsection (3DA), the Registrar or the Minister (as the case may
-- src:5111 | be) must accept as correct any decision of the Court to grant an
-- src:5112 | injunction referred to in subsection (3)(e).
@ref s 28(3E) (src:5104-5112)
GIVEN `the decision is the Registrar's decision under subsection (3) or the Minister's decision under subsection (3DA)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has granted an injunction referred to in subsection (3)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(3E) the Registrar or the Minister must accept as correct the decision of the Court to grant the injunction` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the Registrar's decision under subsection (3) or the Minister's decision under subsection (3DA)` AND `the Court has granted an injunction referred to in subsection (3)(e)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the Registrar makes a decision under subsection (3) or the Minister makes a decision under subsection (3DA), ... must accept as correct any decision of the Court to grant an injunction referred to in subsection (3)(e)" -- outside those decisions the subsection says nothing

§ `Section 28(4) to (6): old names, the certificate, and what a change of name does not change`

-- (4): "Where the name of a company incorporated pursuant to any corresponding previous written law has not been changed since 29 December 1967, the Registrar must not, except with the Minister's approval, exercise the Registrar's power under subsection (3) to direct the company to change its name."
-- A bar gated by "Where": JUST FALSE when the gate fails (the periods ruling, item (b); fork line F-I21), and once the exception is met the text is silent (NOTHING; fork line F-I18).
-- src:5116 | (4) Where the name of a company incorporated pursuant to any
-- src:5117 | corresponding previous written law has not been changed since
-- src:5118 | 29 December 1967, the Registrar must not, except with the Minister’s
-- src:5119 | approval, exercise the Registrar’s power under subsection (3) to
-- src:5120 | direct the company to change its name.
@ref s 28(4) (src:5116-5120)
GIVEN `the company was incorporated pursuant to a corresponding previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the company has not been changed since 29 December 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has approved the exercise of the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(4) the Registrar is barred from directing the company to change its name under subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the company was incorporated pursuant to a corresponding previous written law` AND `the name of the company has not been changed since 29 December 1967`
    THEN (IF `the Minister has approved the exercise of the power`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "except with the Minister's approval" is met; the text then says nothing of whether the Registrar may direct (fork line F-I18)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the name of a company incorporated pursuant to any corresponding previous written law has not been changed since 29 December 1967, the Registrar must not ..." (a bar gated by "Where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-I21)

-- (5): "Upon the application of a company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation of the company under the new name."
-- A duty gated by "Upon": JUST FALSE where the gate fails (the periods ruling, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11).
-- src:5122 | (5) Upon the application of a company and payment of the
-- src:5123 | prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a
-- src:5124 | certificate confirming the incorporation of the company under the
-- src:5125 | new name.
@ref s 28(5) (src:5122-5125)
GIVEN `the company has applied for the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(5) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation under the new name` MEANS
    IF `the company has applied for the certificate` AND `the prescribed fee has been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of a company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate" (a gate with "Upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

DECLARE `s 28(6) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 28(6) the identity of the company`
    `s 28(6) the rights or obligations of the company`
    `s 28(6) the validity of legal proceedings by or against the company`
    `s 28(6) another matter`

-- (6): "A change of name pursuant to this Act does not affect the identity of the company or any rights or obligations of the company or render defective any legal proceedings by or against the company".
-- src:5129 | (6) A change of name pursuant to this Act does not affect the
-- src:5130 | identity of the company or any rights or obligations of the company or
-- src:5131 | render defective any legal proceedings by or against the company,
-- src:5132 | and any legal proceedings that might have been continued or
-- src:5133 | commenced by or against it by its former name may be continued
-- src:5134 | or commenced by or against it by its new name.
@ref s 28(6) (src:5129-5134)
GIVEN `the name was changed pursuant to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 28(6) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(6) the change of name affects the matter` MEANS
    IF `the name was changed pursuant to this Act`
    THEN (CONSIDER matter
          WHEN `s 28(6) another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the identity, the rights or obligations and the legal proceedings, and says nothing of any other matter
          OTHERWISE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the identity of the company or any rights or obligations of the company or render defective any legal proceedings by or against the company"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A change of name pursuant to this Act" -- a change of name made another way is outside the subsection

-- (6), second limb: "any legal proceedings that might have been continued or commenced by or against it by its former name may be continued or commenced by or against it by its new name."
-- src:5129 | (6) A change of name pursuant to this Act does not affect the
-- src:5130 | identity of the company or any rights or obligations of the company or
-- src:5131 | render defective any legal proceedings by or against the company,
-- src:5132 | and any legal proceedings that might have been continued or
-- src:5133 | commenced by or against it by its former name may be continued
-- src:5134 | or commenced by or against it by its new name.
@ref s 28(6) (src:5129-5134)
GIVEN `the name was changed pursuant to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal proceedings might have been continued or commenced by or against the company by its former name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28(6) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company by its new name` MEANS
    IF `the name was changed pursuant to this Act` AND `the legal proceedings might have been continued or commenced by or against the company by its former name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any legal proceedings that might have been continued or commenced by or against it by its former name may be continued or commenced by or against it by its new name" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

§ `Section 29(1) to (4): approval to omit "Limited" or "Berhad"`

-- (1): "Where it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that a proposed limited company is being formed for the purpose of providing recreation or amusement or promoting commerce, industry, art, science, religion, charity, pension or superannuation schemes or any other object useful to the community,
-- that it has some basis of national or general public interest and that it is in a financial position to carry out the objects for which it is to be formed and will apply its profits (if any) or other income in promoting its objects and will prohibit the payment of any dividend to its members, the Registrar may (after requiring, if the Registrar thinks fit, the proposal to be advertised ...)
-- approve that it be registered as a company with limited liability without the addition of the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' to its name, and the company may be registered accordingly."
-- A "may" gated by "Where": NOTHING when the gate fails (grant ruling, limit 1; split site (ii), fork line F-I19).
-- src:5140 | 29.—(1) Where it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that a
-- src:5141 | proposed limited company is being formed for the purpose of
-- src:5142 | providing recreation or amusement or promoting commerce,
-- src:5143 | industry, art, science, religion, charity, pension or superannuation
-- src:5144 | schemes or any other object useful to the community, that it has some
-- src:5145 | basis of national or general public interest and that it is in a financial
-- src:5146 | position to carry out the objects for which it is to be formed and will
-- src:5147 | apply its profits (if any) or other income in promoting its objects and
-- src:5148 | will prohibit the payment of any dividend to its members, the
-- src:5149 | Registrar may (after requiring, if the Registrar thinks fit, the proposal
-- src:5150 | to be advertised in such manner as the Registrar directs either
-- src:5151 | generally or in a particular case) approve that it be registered as a
-- src:5152 | company with limited liability without the addition of the word
-- src:5157 | “Limited” or “Berhad” to its name, and the company may be
-- src:5158 | registered accordingly.
@ref s 29(1) (src:5140-5158)
GIVEN `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that the proposed limited company is being formed for a purpose this subsection lists or another object useful to the community` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that the proposed limited company has some basis of national or general public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that the proposed limited company is in a financial position to carry out the objects for which it is to be formed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that the proposed limited company will apply its profits or other income in promoting its objects and will prohibit the payment of any dividend to its members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) the Registrar may approve that the proposed limited company be registered without the word Limited or Berhad` MEANS
    IF    `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that the proposed limited company is being formed for a purpose this subsection lists or another object useful to the community`
      AND `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that the proposed limited company has some basis of national or general public interest`
      AND `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that the proposed limited company is in a financial position to carry out the objects for which it is to be formed`
      AND `it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that the proposed limited company will apply its profits or other income in promoting its objects and will prohibit the payment of any dividend to its members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where it is proved to the satisfaction of the Registrar that ..., the Registrar may ... approve" -- a power gated by "Where"; split site (ii), fork line F-I19

