      `it is proved to the Registrar's satisfaction that the company has some basis of national or general public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved to the Registrar's satisfaction that the company is in a financial position to carry out the objects for which it was formed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved to the Registrar's satisfaction that by its constitution the company is required to apply its profits or other income in promoting its objects and is prohibited from paying any dividend to its members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(2) the Registrar may grant approval to the company to change its name to a name without the word Limited or Berhad` MEANS
    IF    `it is proved to the Registrar's satisfaction that the objects of the limited company are restricted to those specified in subsection (1) and to objects incidental or conducive thereto`
      AND `it is proved to the Registrar's satisfaction that the company has some basis of national or general public interest`
      AND `it is proved to the Registrar's satisfaction that the company is in a financial position to carry out the objects for which it was formed`
      AND `it is proved to the Registrar's satisfaction that by its constitution the company is required to apply its profits or other income in promoting its objects and is prohibited from paying any dividend to its members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
