GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 29(3) act`
`s 29(3) the company must insert the conditions in its constitution if the Registrar so directs` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 29(3) insert the conditions in the constitution of the company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 29(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not insert in its constitution the conditions the Registrar directed it to insert" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

