§ `Section 29(5) to (13): the exemption, its revocation, appeals and transitional rules`

-- (5): "A company is, while an approval granted under this section to it is in force, exempted from complying with the provisions of this Act relating to the use of the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' as any part of its name."
-- A status "while" the approval is in force: JUST FALSE outside it (the periods ruling, item (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; fork line F-I22).
-- src:5201 | (5) A company is, while an approval granted under this section to it
-- src:5202 | is in force, exempted from complying with the provisions of this Act
-- src:5203 | relating to the use of the word “Limited” or “Berhad” as any part of its
-- src:5204 | name.
@ref s 29(5) (src:5201-5204)
GIVEN `an approval granted under section 29 to the company is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(5) the company is exempted from complying with the provisions of this Act relating to the use of the word Limited or Berhad` MEANS
    IF `an approval granted under section 29 to the company is in force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while an approval granted under this section to it is in force, exempted" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); fork line F-I22)

-- (6): "Any approval granted under this section may at any time be revoked by the Registrar and, upon revocation, the Registrar must enter the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' at the end of the name of the company in the register, and the company must thereupon cease to enjoy the exemption granted by reason of the approval under this section
-- but before the approval is so revoked the Registrar must give to the company written notice of the Registrar's intention and must afford it an opportunity to be heard."
-- The power to revoke: the precondition is a duty ("must give ... notice", "must afford ... an opportunity to be heard"), not an "only if": NOTHING where it is not met (fork line F-I23).
-- src:5209 | (6) Any approval granted under this section may at any time be
-- src:5210 | revoked by the Registrar and, upon revocation, the Registrar must
-- src:5211 | enter the word “Limited” or “Berhad” at the end of the name of the
-- src:5212 | company in the register, and the company must thereupon cease to
-- src:5213 | enjoy the exemption granted by reason of the approval under this
-- src:5214 | section but before the approval is so revoked the Registrar must give
-- src:5215 | to the company written notice of the Registrar’s intention and must
-- src:5216 | afford it an opportunity to be heard.
@ref s 29(6) (src:5209-5216)
GIVEN `an approval granted under section 29 to the company is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has given the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has afforded the company an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(6) the Registrar may revoke the approval` MEANS
    IF    `an approval granted under section 29 to the company is in force`
      AND `the Registrar has given the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke`
      AND `the Registrar has afforded the company an opportunity to be heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may at any time be revoked by the Registrar ... but before the approval is so revoked the Registrar must give ... written notice ... and must afford ... an opportunity to be heard" -- the precondition is phrased as a duty, not as "only if" (fork line F-I23)

-- src:5209 | (6) Any approval granted under this section may at any time be
-- src:5210 | revoked by the Registrar and, upon revocation, the Registrar must
-- src:5211 | enter the word “Limited” or “Berhad” at the end of the name of the
-- src:5212 | company in the register, and the company must thereupon cease to
-- src:5213 | enjoy the exemption granted by reason of the approval under this
-- src:5214 | section but before the approval is so revoked the Registrar must give
-- src:5215 | to the company written notice of the Registrar’s intention and must
-- src:5216 | afford it an opportunity to be heard.
@ref s 29(6) (src:5209-5216)
GIVEN `the Registrar revokes the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(6) before the revocation the Registrar must give the company written notice and afford it an opportunity to be heard` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar revokes the approval`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the approval is so revoked" -- where the Registrar does not revoke, the text names no duty

-- src:5209 | (6) Any approval granted under this section may at any time be
-- src:5210 | revoked by the Registrar and, upon revocation, the Registrar must
-- src:5211 | enter the word “Limited” or “Berhad” at the end of the name of the
-- src:5212 | company in the register, and the company must thereupon cease to
-- src:5213 | enjoy the exemption granted by reason of the approval under this
-- src:5214 | section but before the approval is so revoked the Registrar must give
-- src:5215 | to the company written notice of the Registrar’s intention and must
-- src:5216 | afford it an opportunity to be heard.
@ref s 29(6) (src:5209-5216)
GIVEN `the Registrar has revoked the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(6) upon the revocation the Registrar must enter the word Limited or Berhad at the end of the name in the register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has revoked the approval`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon revocation, the Registrar must enter the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' at the end of the name of the company in the register" (a duty gated by "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

-- src:5209 | (6) Any approval granted under this section may at any time be
-- src:5210 | revoked by the Registrar and, upon revocation, the Registrar must
-- src:5211 | enter the word “Limited” or “Berhad” at the end of the name of the
-- src:5212 | company in the register, and the company must thereupon cease to
-- src:5213 | enjoy the exemption granted by reason of the approval under this
-- src:5214 | section but before the approval is so revoked the Registrar must give
-- src:5215 | to the company written notice of the Registrar’s intention and must
-- src:5216 | afford it an opportunity to be heard.
@ref s 29(6) (src:5209-5216)
GIVEN `the Registrar has revoked the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(6) upon the revocation the company ceases to enjoy the exemption` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has revoked the approval`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon revocation, ... the company must thereupon cease to enjoy the exemption granted by reason of the approval" (a status gated by "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

-- (6A): "If the Registrar is of the opinion that a company has ceased to satisfy the conditions of approval granted under subsection (1) or (2), the Registrar may revoke the approval."
-- src:5220 | (6A) If the Registrar is of the opinion that a company has ceased to
-- src:5221 | satisfy the conditions of approval granted under subsection (1) or (2),
-- src:5222 | the Registrar may revoke the approval.
@ref s 29(6A) (src:5220-5222)
GIVEN `the Registrar is of the opinion that the company has ceased to satisfy the conditions of approval granted under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(6A) the Registrar may revoke the approval` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is of the opinion that the company has ceased to satisfy the conditions of approval granted under subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Registrar is of the opinion that a company has ceased to satisfy the conditions ..., the Registrar may revoke the approval" -- a power whose "If" gate failed; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-I2)

-- (7): "Where the approval of the Registrar under this section is revoked, the constitution of the company may be altered by special resolution so as to remove any provision in or to the effect that the constitution may be altered only with the consent of the Minister."
-- src:5226 | (7) Where the approval of the Registrar under this section is
-- src:5227 | revoked, the constitution of the company may be altered by special
-- src:5228 | resolution so as to remove any provision in or to the effect that the
-- src:5229 | constitution may be altered only with the consent of the Minister.
@ref s 29(7) (src:5226-5229)
GIVEN `the approval of the Registrar under this section is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(7) the constitution may be altered by special resolution to remove the provision requiring the Minister's consent` MEANS
    IF `the approval of the Registrar under this section is revoked` AND `the resolution is a special resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the approval ... is revoked, the constitution of the company may be altered by special resolution so as to remove any provision ..." -- a permission gated by "Where"; the text names no outcome where it is not met (fork line F-I2)

-- (8): "Notice of any approval under this section must be given by the Registrar to the company or, in the case of a proposed limited company, to the applicant for the approval."
-- The notice is owed to the company or the applicant. Another person: the text does not say (NOTHING). No approval: no notice owed under this subsection (JUST FALSE; the provision's own question).
-- src:5233 | (8) Notice of any approval under this section must be given by the
-- src:5234 | Registrar to the company or, in the case of a proposed limited
-- src:5235 | company, to the applicant for the approval.
@ref s 29(8) (src:5233-5235)
GIVEN `the Registrar has approved under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or, in the case of a proposed limited company, the applicant for the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(8) the notice of the approval must be given to the person` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has approved under this section`
    THEN (IF `the person is the company or, in the case of a proposed limited company, the applicant for the approval`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be given by the Registrar to the company or, in the case of a proposed limited company, to the applicant for the approval" -- the text names no other person
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notice of any approval under this section must be given" (a duty whose object is an approval: where there is none the duty does not arise; the provision's own question, fork line F-I21)

DECLARE `s 29(8A) decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 29(8A)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (1)`
    `s 29(8A)(b) the Registrar's decision under subsection (2)`
    `s 29(8A) another decision`

-- (8A): "An appeal to the Minister against a decision of the Registrar under subsection (1) or (2) may be made by the following persons within the following times: (a) in the case of a decision under subsection (1) — by the promoter of the proposed limited company within 30 days after the notice is given by the Registrar under subsection (8);
-- (b) in the case of a decision under subsection (2) — by the company within 30 days after the notice is given by the Registrar under subsection (8)."
-- src:5239 | (8A) An appeal to the Minister against a decision of the Registrar
-- src:5240 | under subsection (1) or (2) may be made by the following persons
-- src:5241 | within the following times:
-- src:5243 | (a) in the case of a decision made by the Registrar under
-- src:5244 | subsection (1) — by the promoter of the proposed limited
-- src:5245 | company within 30 days after the notice is given by the
-- src:5246 | Registrar under subsection (8);
-- src:5248 | (b) in the case of a decision made by the Registrar under
-- src:5249 | subsection (2) — by the company within 30 days after the
-- src:5250 | notice is given by the Registrar under subsection (8).
@ref s 29(8A) (src:5239-5250)
GIVEN decision IS A `s 29(8A) decision`
      `the person is the promoter of the proposed limited company, for a decision under subsection (1), or the company, for a decision under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Registrar gave the notice under subsection (8)` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(8A) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` MEANS
    IF decision EQUALS `s 29(8A) another decision`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (8A) names decisions under subsections (1) and (2) and says nothing of any other
    ELSE (IF `the person is the promoter of the proposed limited company, for a decision under subsection (1), or the company, for a decision under subsection (2)`
          THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the Registrar gave the notice under subsection (8)` `the day the appeal is made` 30 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after the notice is given by the Registrar under subsection (8)" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the promoter of the proposed limited company" / "by the company" -- the text names no other person

-- (9): "Upon the application of the company or proposed limited company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company or proposed limited company a certificate confirming the approval under this section."
-- src:5254 | (9) Upon the application of the company or proposed limited
-- src:5255 | company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue
-- src:5256 | to the company or proposed limited company a certificate confirming
-- src:5257 | the approval under this section.
@ref s 29(9) (src:5254-5257)
GIVEN `the company or proposed limited company has applied for the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(9) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the approval` MEANS
    IF `the company or proposed limited company has applied for the certificate` AND `the prescribed fee has been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of the company or proposed limited company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue ... a certificate" (a gate with "Upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

-- (10): "This section does not apply to a limited company that is registered as a charity under the Charities Act 1994."
-- src:5262 | (10) This section does not apply to a limited company that is
-- src:5263 | registered as a charity under the Charities Act 1994.
@ref s 29(10) (src:5262-5263)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is registered as a charity under the Charities Act 1994` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(10) section 29 applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "limited company" the company is a limited company` liability `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the company is registered as a charity under the Charities Act 1994`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to a limited company that is registered as a charity under the Charities Act 1994."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection excludes one kind of company and says nothing of any other

-- (11), (12) and (13) are transitional: what was done or said before 3 January 2016 is, on or after that date, read as the Registrar's. Before that date the text does not carry it over (JUST FALSE: a date the text fixes in its own words); where no such approval, condition or reference exists, the text names nothing (NOTHING). Fork line F-I24.
-- src:5267 | (11) Any approval of the Minister and any condition of the
-- src:5268 | Minister’s approval that was in force immediately before 3 January
-- src:5269 | 2016 for a company —
-- src:5271 | (a) to be registered without the word “Limited” or “Berhad” to
-- src:5272 | its name; or
-- src:5274 | (b) to change its name to one which does not contain the word
-- src:5275 | “Limited” or “Berhad”,
-- src:5277 | is on or after that date to be treated as the approval of the Registrar
-- src:5278 | and condition of the Registrar’s approval.
@ref s 29(11) (src:5267-5278)
GIVEN `the Minister's approval, or a condition of it, was in force immediately before 3 January 2016 for the company to be registered without the word Limited or Berhad, or to change its name to one without it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(11) the approval or condition is treated as the Registrar's approval and condition` MEANS
    IF `the Minister's approval, or a condition of it, was in force immediately before 3 January 2016 for the company to be registered without the word Limited or Berhad, or to change its name to one without it`
    THEN (IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is on or after that date to be treated as the approval of the Registrar" (a date the text fixes in its own words; fork line F-I24)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any approval of the Minister and any condition of the Minister's approval that was in force immediately before 3 January 2016" -- an approval or condition not then in force is outside the subsection

-- src:5282 | (12) Any reference to the Minister’s approval in any condition of
-- src:5283 | approval that was in force immediately before 3 January 2016 that
-- src:5284 | was inserted in the constitution of a company pursuant to a direction
-- src:5285 | of the Minister under section 29(3) in force immediately before that
-- src:5286 | date is, on or after that date, to be read as a reference to the Registrar.
@ref s 29(12) (src:5282-5286)
GIVEN `the reference to the Minister's approval is in a condition of approval that was in force immediately before 3 January 2016 and was inserted in the constitution pursuant to a direction of the Minister under section 29(3) in force immediately before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(12) the reference to the Minister's approval is read as a reference to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the reference to the Minister's approval is in a condition of approval that was in force immediately before 3 January 2016 and was inserted in the constitution pursuant to a direction of the Minister under section 29(3) in force immediately before that date`
    THEN (IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, on or after that date, to be read as a reference to the Registrar" (a date the text fixes in its own words; fork line F-I24)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any reference to the Minister's approval in any condition of approval that was in force immediately before 3 January 2016 that was inserted in the constitution ... pursuant to a direction of the Minister" -- another reference is outside the subsection

-- src:5290 | (13) A reference to a direction of the Minister in subsections (3) and
-- src:5291 | (4) in force immediately before 3 January 2016 is, on or after that
-- src:5292 | date, to be read as a direction of the Registrar.
@ref s 29(13) (src:5290-5292)
GIVEN `the reference is to a direction of the Minister in subsection (3) or (4) in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(13) the reference to a direction of the Minister is read as a direction of the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to a direction of the Minister in subsection (3) or (4) in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
    THEN (IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, on or after that date, to be read as a direction of the Registrar" (a date the text fixes in its own words; fork line F-I24)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A reference to a direction of the Minister in subsections (3) and (4) in force immediately before 3 January 2016" -- another reference is outside the subsection

§ `Section 29A: charitable companies omitting "Limited" or "Berhad"`

-- (1): "Despite section 28(1) and (2) but subject to section 28(3) to (6), a limited company registered as a charity under the Charities Act 1994 (called in this section a charitable company) may change its name to omit the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' from its name."
-- "Subject to section 28(3) to (6)" points outside the subsection to the limits those provisions set; they are answered in their own functions above (fork line F-I25).
-- src:5299 | 29A.—(1) Despite section 28(1) and (2) but subject to section 28(3)
-- src:5300 | to (6), a limited company registered as a charity under the Charities
-- src:5301 | Act 1994 (called in this section a charitable company) may change its
-- src:5302 | name to omit the word “Limited” or “Berhad” from its name.
@ref s 29A(1) (src:5299-5302)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is registered as a charity under the Charities Act 1994` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(1) the charitable company may change its name to omit the word Limited or Berhad` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "limited company" the company is a limited company` liability `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the company is registered as a charity under the Charities Act 1994`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a limited company registered as a charity under the Charities Act 1994 ... may change its name to omit the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad'" -- a permission whose subject is not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

DECLARE `s 29A(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 29A(2)(a) alter the constitution to reflect the change of name`
    `s 29A(2)(b) file the prescribed form with the Registrar, together with a copy of the special resolution authorising the change of name`

-- (2): "A charitable company that proposes to change its name to omit the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' from its name must — (a) alter its constitution to reflect the change of name; and (b) file the prescribed form with the Registrar, together with a copy of the special resolution authorising the change of name."
-- No time is fixed, so neither duty can reach BREACH (listed in NOTES.md under "Rules with no breach path").
-- src:5306 | (2) A charitable company that proposes to change its name to omit
-- src:5307 | the word “Limited” or “Berhad” from its name must —
-- src:5309 | (a) alter its constitution to reflect the change of name; and
-- src:5314 | (b) file the prescribed form with the Registrar, together with a
-- src:5315 | copy of the special resolution authorising the change of
-- src:5316 | name.
@ref s 29A(2) (src:5306-5316)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 29A(2) act`
`s 29A(2)(a) the charitable company must alter its constitution to reflect the change of name` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 29A(2)(a) alter the constitution to reflect the change of name`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 29A(2)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the charitable company did not alter its constitution to reflect the change of name" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:5306 | (2) A charitable company that proposes to change its name to omit
-- src:5307 | the word “Limited” or “Berhad” from its name must —
-- src:5309 | (a) alter its constitution to reflect the change of name; and
-- src:5314 | (b) file the prescribed form with the Registrar, together with a
-- src:5315 | copy of the special resolution authorising the change of
-- src:5316 | name.
@ref s 29A(2) (src:5306-5316)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 29A(2) act`
`s 29A(2)(b) the charitable company must file the prescribed form with the Registrar and a copy of the special resolution` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 29A(2)(b) file the prescribed form with the Registrar, together with a copy of the special resolution authorising the change of name`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 29A(2)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the charitable company did not file the prescribed form with the Registrar together with a copy of the special resolution authorising the change of name" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:5306 | (2) A charitable company that proposes to change its name to omit
-- src:5307 | the word “Limited” or “Berhad” from its name must —
-- src:5309 | (a) alter its constitution to reflect the change of name; and
-- src:5314 | (b) file the prescribed form with the Registrar, together with a
-- src:5315 | copy of the special resolution authorising the change of
-- src:5316 | name.
@ref s 29A(2) (src:5306-5316)
GIVEN `the company is a charitable company that proposes to change its name to omit the word Limited or Berhad` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has altered its constitution to reflect the change of name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has filed the prescribed form with the Registrar together with a copy of the special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(2) the charitable company has met the requirements for the change of name` MEANS
    IF `the company is a charitable company that proposes to change its name to omit the word Limited or Berhad`
    THEN (IF `the company has altered its constitution to reflect the change of name` AND `the company has filed the prescribed form with the Registrar together with a copy of the special resolution`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection fixes no time, so it does not say that a company still to do (a) or (b) has failed
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A charitable company that proposes to change its name ... must" (a duty gated by "that proposes": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; fork line F-I21)

-- (3): "Upon receipt of the prescribed form mentioned in subsection (2)(b), the Registrar must — (a) register the name of the charitable company with the omission of the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' from its name; and (b) issue to the company a notice of incorporation of the company under the new name."
-- src:5320 | (3) Upon receipt of the prescribed form mentioned in
-- src:5321 | subsection (2)(b), the Registrar must —
-- src:5323 | (a) register the name of the charitable company with the
-- src:5324 | omission of the word “Limited” or “Berhad” from its
-- src:5325 | name; and
-- src:5327 | (b) issue to the company a notice of incorporation of the
-- src:5328 | company under the new name.
@ref s 29A(3) (src:5320-5328)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received the prescribed form mentioned in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(3) the Registrar must register the name of the charitable company with the omission and issue the notice of incorporation` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received the prescribed form mentioned in subsection (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon receipt of the prescribed form ..., the Registrar must — (a) register ...; and (b) issue ..." (a gate with "Upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

-- (4): "Upon issue of the notice under subsection (3)(b) — (a) the change of name becomes effective; and (b) the charitable company is exempted from the provisions of this Act relating to the use of the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' as part of the name."
-- src:5332 | (4) Upon issue of the notice under subsection (3)(b) —
-- src:5334 | (a) the change of name becomes effective; and
-- src:5336 | (b) the charitable company is exempted from the provisions of
-- src:5337 | this Act relating to the use of the word “Limited” or
-- src:5338 | “Berhad” as part of the name.
@ref s 29A(4) (src:5332-5338)
GIVEN `the Registrar has issued the notice under subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was issued` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(4) the change of name has become effective and the charitable company is exempted` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has issued the notice under subsection (3)(b)` AND `the date asked` AT LEAST `the day the notice was issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon issue of the notice under subsection (3)(b) — (a) the change of name becomes effective; and (b) the charitable company is exempted" (a status gated by "Upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

-- (5): "If the Registrar is satisfied that a charitable company that is registered with the omission of the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' from its name under this section has ceased to be a charitable company, the Registrar must enter the word 'Limited' or 'Berhad' at the end of the name of the company
-- and upon notice of that fact being given to the company, the exemption under subsection (4)(b) ceases."
-- src:5342 | (5) If the Registrar is satisfied that a charitable company that is
-- src:5343 | registered with the omission of the word “Limited” or “Berhad” from
-- src:5344 | its name under this section has ceased to be a charitable company, the
