-- src:5346 | name of the company and upon notice of that fact being given to the
-- src:5347 | company, the exemption under subsection (4)(b) ceases.
@ref s 29A(5) (src:5342-5347)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the company, registered with the omission of the word Limited or Berhad under section 29A, has ceased to be a charitable company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(5) the Registrar must enter the word Limited or Berhad at the end of the name of the company` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the company, registered with the omission of the word Limited or Berhad under section 29A, has ceased to be a charitable company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Registrar is satisfied that a charitable company ... has ceased to be a charitable company, the Registrar must enter the word" (a duty gated by "If": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; fork line F-I21)

